**Given:**

x = frac{{sqrt{5} + 1}}{{sqrt{5} - 1}}

y = (1)/(x)

**Formula used:**

To find x² + y², use:

x = frac{{sqrt{5} + 1}}{{sqrt{5} - 1}}

y = (1)/(x)

**Calculations:**

x = frac{{sqrt{5} + 1}}{{sqrt{5} - 1}}

⇒ Multiply numerator and denominator by (sqrt{5} + 1):

x = frac{{(sqrt{5} + 1)²}}{{(sqrt{5} - 1)(sqrt{5} + 1)}}

⇒ (sqrt{5} - 1)(sqrt{5} + 1) = 5 - 1 = 4

⇒ (sqrt{5} + 1)² = 5 + 2sqrt{5} + 1 = 6 + 2sqrt{5}

x = frac{6 + 2sqrt{5}}{4} = frac{3 + sqrt{5}}{2}

y = (2)/(3 + sqrt{5)}

⇒ Multiply numerator and denominator by (3 - sqrt{5}):

y = frac{2(3 - sqrt{5})}{(3 + sqrt{5})(3 - sqrt{5})}

⇒ (3 + sqrt{5})(3 - sqrt{5}) = 9 - 5 = 4

⇒ y = frac{2(3 - sqrt{5})}{4} = frac{3 - sqrt{5}}{2}

x² = (frac{3 + sqrt{5}}{2})² = frac{(3 + sqrt{5})²}{4} = frac{9 + 6sqrt{5} + 5}{4} = frac{14 + 6sqrt{5}}{4} = frac{7 + 3sqrt{5}}{2}

y² = (frac{3 - sqrt{5}}{2})² = frac{(3 - sqrt{5})²}{4} = frac{9 - 6sqrt{5} + 5}{4} = frac{14 - 6sqrt{5}}{4} = frac{7 - 3sqrt{5}}{2}

x² + y² = frac{7 + 3sqrt{5}}{2} + frac{7 - 3sqrt{5}}{2} = (14)/(2) = 7

**∴ The value of x² + y² is 7.**

**Given:**

Side of the equilateral triangle = 2√2 cm.

**Formula Used:**

Length of perpendicular (height) in an equilateral triangle = frac{sqrt{3}}{2} times {side} 

**Calculation:**

Side = 2√2 cm

Length of perpendicular (height) = frac{sqrt{3}}{2} times 2sqrt{2} 

⇒ Length of perpendicular (height) = sqrt{3} times sqrt{2} 

⇒ Length of perpendicular (height) = sqrt{6} 

**The length of the perpendicular drawn from vertex to the side is √6 cm.**
